        "original_id": "195108f3-0f47-5082-a021-f21059bcc5fd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Garth Brooks, Dewayne Blackwell, Victoria Shaw, David Frizzell\n- Songs: \"Friends in Low Places\", \"She's Every Woman\", \"Mr. Blue\", \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\"\n- Albums: \"No Fences\"\n- Charts: Billboard Top Country Albums\n\nFacts:\n- In 1959, the song \"Mr. Blue,\" written by Dewayne Blackwell, was a hit for the Fleetwoods.\n- In 1982, the song \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home,\" written by Dewayne Blackwell, was a hit for David Frizzell.\n- On August 6, 1990, Garth Brooks released \"Friends in Low Places\" as the lead single from the album \"No Fences.\"\n- In 1990, \"Friends in Low Places\" was a hit for Garth Brooks, and Dewayne Blackwell was one of its songwriters.\n- On August 27, 1990, Garth Brooks released the album \"No Fences.\"\n- The album \"No Fences\" reached number 1 on Billboard's Top Country Albums chart.\n- Garth Brooks performed the song \"Friends in Low Places\" as an American country pop artist.\n- Victoria Shaw and Garth Brooks wrote the song \"She's Every Woman,\" and Brooks recorded it.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "63f24378-1119-562e-98cc-245f56d9adfc",
        "text": "Page: Friends in Low Places. Sentence: \"Friends in Low Places\" is a song performed by American country pop artist Garth Brooks.\nPage: Friends in Low Places. Sentence: It was released on August 6, 1990 as the lead single from his album \"No Fences\".\nPage: No Fences. Sentence: It was released on August 27, 1990, and reached #1 on \"Billboard's\" Top Country Albums chart.\nPage: Dewayne Blackwell. Sentence: His songs include \"Mr. Blue\", a 1959 hit for the Fleetwoods; \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\", a 1982 hit for David Frizzell; and \"Friends in Low Places\", a 1990 hit for Garth Brooks.\nPage: She's Every Woman. Sentence: \"She's Every Woman\" is a song written by Victoria Shaw and Garth Brooks, and recorded by Brooks.",
